for more than 250 years it's been a key  ingredient of French cuisine we're going  to make a typical French mousse au  chocolat using my mother's recipe as a  patissier Cyril jaha knows his way  around French desserts for the past two  and a half years he's been working at  the luxury hotel and restaurant or  beverage Dubois in the French ski resort  of Sharm Oni that's right across from  Mont Blanc the tallest mountain in  Europe stealing Jetta takes care of the  sweet stuff while the lunch is being  prepared he only needs four ingredients  sugar butter chocolate and eggs  first he melts the butter and chocolate  in a pan it's really important that the  chocolate isn't too cold otherwise it  will harden again when you mix it with  the egg yolk he recommends using  chocolate with a high percentage of  cocoa you can buy the chocolate for the  mousse in any supermarket but it should  be at least 50% cocoa the lower the  percentage the more chocolate you'll  need to use the jedis using chocolate  with 66% cocoa the danique Xavier owns  the restaurant he usually orders in bulk  but today he's shopping in a local  chocolate shop  the shaka latinos what makes a good  moose you can use all types of chocolate  it's all about the balance if you use a  very strong chocolate then you need a  lot of sugar to counter the bitterness  but you can make a mousse out of any  kind of chocolate when the dark of white  or milk chocolate meanwhile syria has  melted the chocolate and he is now  separating the eggs he mixes the yolks  with sugar it's important to stir for a  long time so the sugar binds with the  yolk the yolks would be a little foamy  then he beats the egg whites and mixes  the melted chocolate with the egg yolk  the egg whites shouldn't be beaten too  long if the egg white is too stiff then  it will flake later he gently folds a  bit of egg white into the chocolate mix  to lighten it then he slowly adds the  rest  fold it carefully so that the egg white  doesn't fall in on itself the mousse has  to stay really light the dessert is  almost ready  it just has to cool in the fridge for  three hours to firm it up a little in  the end the mousse should be Aryan not  too heavy otherwise it will just get  slushy mousse au chocolat is always the  right choice every day all year round  it's a gourmets dessert for Igor mousse  au chocolat every day now there's a  sweet temptation
 

